  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "check_content_type_and_change_protocol",
    "file": "ndpi/src/lib/protocols/http.c",
    "description": "The root cause is an unsafe call site that passes a non-NUL-terminated, length-delimited header buffer to ndpi_strncasestr(). In check_content_type_and_change_protocol(), packet->authorization_line.ptr is searched for \"Basic\"/\"Digest\" with ndpi_strncasestr(..., packet->authorization_line.len). ndpi_strncasestr() computes str1_len via strnlen but then iterates with `for(i = 0; i < (str1_len - str2_len + 1); i++)` without handling `str1_len < str2_len`, causing size_t underflow and an over-read via str1[0]/strncasecmp past the provided buffer.",
    "conditions": "Triggered during HTTP parsing in fuzz_process_packet when an Authorization header is present with short/empty value (or otherwise shorter than the needle \"Basic\"/\"Digest\") and not guaranteed NUL-terminated. Flow: input packet -> ndpi_detection_process_packet -> ndpi_search_http_tcp/ndpi_check_http_tcp -> check_content_type_and_change_protocol -> ndpi_strncasestr on authorization_line. If authorization_line.len < strlen(\"Basic\") (or < strlen(\"Digest\")), ndpi_strncasestr loop bound underflows and reads beyond heap buffer end."
  },
